'''bent'''<sup>1</sup> (bent), ''n.'' [Var. of ''bend''<sup>1</sup>, ''n.'', perhaps after ''bent''<sup>1</sup>, pret. and pp.; but cf. ''descent,'' < ''descend; ascent,'' < ''ascend,'' etc.] '''1.''' The state of being bent; curved form or position; flexure; curvature. [Now rare.]
