{{right|''I. Walton,'' Complete Angler.}}}}
'''2†.''' A curved part; a crook or bend.—'''3.''' Degree of flexure or curvature; tension; straining; utmost force or power: an archery expression, but used figuratively of mental disposition.
{{smaller block|Her affections have their full ''bent.''
{{right|''Shak.,'' Much Ado, ii. 3.}}
